From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:53:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] mtd: apple-sftl: Describe the package geometry at
 runtime

The translation layer fixes the measured 64 GB package in compile-time
constants: 16 lanes, 128 pages per block, 2088 physical blocks, 2086
superblocks, the VFL bootstrap block 2087 and members from block 2056,
64 SLC pages per VFL bank and 15625016 logical pages. The 16 GB P105
package uses the same VFL and SwissPPNFTL structures with other values,
so a second package cannot be added without touching every bound.

Select a geometry descriptor from the provider's bus, CAU, block and
page counts and derive the address stride, provider size, slot counts and
range sentinel from it. Arrays keep the 64 GB maxima. The native context
tag check gains a variant that sizes the block table, user sequence and
read count sections from the superblock count; the 64 GB layout it
produces is unchanged.

The writer, reclamation, VFL rotation and snapshots keep the 64 GB
address layout of the reclaim and accounting code. A descriptor states
whether that writer is modelled for it; one that is not exposes its disk
read-only.

The 64 GB descriptor reproduces every previous constant. No functional
change.

Assisted-by: LLM
